WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.400
If I don’t think the future
is worth anything

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.880
then I'm not going to have children.
If I think it is worth something,

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:05.840
I will have children.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.840
We are already seeing
coastal city flooding,

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.320
we're already seeing forest fires,
we're already seeing flash floods,

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.600
we're seeing tornadoes.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.920
When big ecological disasters
happen around the world,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.720
I feel a sense of anxiety.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.720
I feel a sense of sadness
and a sense of loss.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.240
So imagine you go outside
and you look up in the sky,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.360
and there's a comet there.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.880
And you know - you've just
been told by scientists

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.440
that that comet
is racing toward the Earth

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.680
and it's going to kill everybody
and everything in a big fiery storm.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.480
And nobody else notices the comet.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.760
And you say: "Hey look,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.880
there's a comet and it's
going to kill all of us..."

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.760
And people just don’t seem to care.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:53.560
Climate change anxiety as a term
is a relatively new term.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.880
By no way a new phenomenon.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.200
It's an anxiety that
is about the future.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.120
And a trauma that we haven't
experienced yet,

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.200
but that we know is going to
come our way.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.400
We're facing a very existential fear.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.360
This is not a fear about how
does my body look?

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.120
Or am I popular enough?

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.160
This is a fear about our survival.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.920
What is it that makes you anxious?

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:44.080
What are the thoughts or what are
the details that when you go there

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.000
that's when you touch your anxiety.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.520
In other parts of the world,

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.920
they'll be more affected
by climate change

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.480
than the cities that
we currently live in.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.600
That's when I feel like...

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.120
we're not doing enough.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.720
One of the most

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.440
sort of potent anxieties,
is the fear of...

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.160
people mistreating each other
out of panic and fear

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.160
and, you know...

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.840
it's more maybe how people
respond to that.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.800
I just keep thinking about...

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.320
a small child.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:29.400
Probably myself.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.080
And I just think about how

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.360
innocent my -
god I'm emotional already.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.040
That memory I have of being a child,

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.680
that is so valuable.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.640
And I just think about all the people
that aren't... That don't have that.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.560
That preciousness about the world
and I think that’s really...

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.320
That's a privilege
that is just disappearing.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.000
Yeah I get emotional
when I think about...

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:59.360
the effects that climate change
and its related issues will have.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.600
I get very angry about those,
I feel very powerless.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.920
I feel very frustrated.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.760
I think we need more and more
people to wake up to this

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.240
and anxiety is part of the way

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.920
of digesting the information,
there's no way around that.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.560
What is the part that you can play
in stretching out

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.360
and mending the part of the world
that is within your reach?

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:27.120
In the face of constant defeat,
just stubbornness and tenacity.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.760
Understand what your impact
as a human being

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.040
is on the planet.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.160
I feel so helpless but...

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.240
But so empowered by that helplessness

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.760
that I then want to try
and do everything and so.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.320
We see and an unprecedented
amount of people

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.880
who present with anxiety
that they can't even locate.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.560
And I'm wondering whether this is
that people are actually picking up

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.480
that something is not right.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.000
I don't think it's all...

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.480
I have to believe it's not all bad.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.080
Maybe things will be fixed
by the time they're an adult

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.120
and it will be all good.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.600
I feel the most hopeful
when I remind myself

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.240
how bad humans have always
been at predicting the future.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.820
Thanks for watching ;)

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:23.120
